3. Regent is the Regent of Jombang;
4. Regional House of Representatives hereinafter referred to as DPRD is the regional people's representative institution as an element of regional government administration;
5. Regional Governance is the administration of government affairs by the Regional Government and DPRD according to the principles of Autonomy and assistance duties with the principle of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia as referred to in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
6. Agency is the Regional Work Unit whose main duties and functions include the fields of social affairs, women's empowerment and child protection;
7. Child is a person who has not yet reached 18 years of age, including those in the womb;
8. Violence is any act that results in or may result in misery or suffering to the victim;
9. Physical violence is any act that causes pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or causes death;
10. Psychological violence is an act that causes fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering to a person:

11.Sexual violence is any act in the form of sexual harassment, forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural manner or unwanted against another person whether for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes;

12. Victim is a Woman and Child who experiences misery and or suffering as a result of violence;

13. Protection is all efforts aimed at providing a sense of security to victims either temporarily or based on a Court decision;

14. Service is an action that must be immediately taken for the victim when seeing, hearing and reasonably suspected that violence against the victim will, is, or has occurred; 15. Companion is a person or representative of an institution who has the expertise to accompany victims in conducting counseling, therapy and advocacy for the strengthening and recovery of victims of violence;

16. Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children hereinafter referred to as P2T-P2A is a service provider institution based in a Hospital for victims of violence especially women and children that is managed jointly by the regional government and the community incorporated in a Team carried out across functions and across sectors in the form of medical services (including medico-legal), psycho-social and legal services;

17. Safe house is a temporary residence used to provide protection to victims; 18. Community is individuals, individuals, families, groups, communities and social organizations;

19. Family is the smallest unit in society consisting of husband-wife, or husband-wife and their children, or father and their children, and mother and their children;

20. Household is family members and relatives (a person who has a blood relationship with family members) and non-relatives, who live and eat from one kitchen and reside in one house.

Article 9

Paragraph (1) What is meant by fast, safe, empathetic, non-discriminatory, easily accessible and with guaranteed confidentiality in the handling/examination of women and children victims of violence, victims are examined at the P2T-P2A Secretariat or Women and Children Protection Unit (UPPA) Room, which is a special closed and comfortable room in the Police Unit, where women and children victims of domestic violence and sexual violence or harassment can report their cases safely to female police officers who are empathetic, understanding and professional.

Paragraph (2) What is meant by no fees charged is that there is an exemption of visum fees free of charge for women and children victims of physical and sexual violence which can be done at the Regional General Hospital of Jombang Regency as well as at the Community Health Center (PUSKESMAS) with a visum letter from the Police, which is further stipulated in the Technical Manual;

